ees; on-linear regression and polynomial regression. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundametals of Machine Learning task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Mathematics equations for Machine learning is covered under the syllabus unit “Unit 1”. Define the concept, explain its role and main components or steps, connect it to Basic introduction to linear algebra, Matrices, vectors in linear algebra, Unit 1, provide a practical course-related example and state one validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Basic introduction to linear algebra; Matrices; vectors in linear algebra; Unit 1. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundametals of Machine Learning task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

