VALUES (4400093516060129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Fundametals of Machine Learning requires the behaviour described by the syllabus area concerned with Basic introduction to linear algebra. Explain how Basic introduction to linear algebra applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Fundametals of Machine Learning requires the behaviour described by the syllabus area concerned with What is machine learning. Explain how What is machine learning applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Fundametals of Machine Learning requires the behaviour described by a model learns input-to-target relationships from labelled training examples. Explain how How supervised learning works. Types of Supervised learning applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Fundametals of Machine Learning requires the behaviour described by a model learns input-to-target relationships from labelled training examples. Explain how what is unsupervised learning and working of unsupervised learning applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Basic introduction to linear algebra is covered under the syllabus unit “Unit 1”. Define the concept, explain its role and main components or steps, connect it to Mathematics equations for Machine learning, Matrices, vectors in linear algebra, Unit 1, provide a practical course-related example and state one validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Mathematics equations for Machine learning; Matrices; vectors in linear algebra; Unit 1. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundametals of Machine Learning task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** What is machine learning is covered under the syllabus unit “Unit 2”. Define the concept, explain its role and main components or steps, connect it to classification, Machine learning lifecycle, Different applications of ML, Difference between AI and machine learning Machine Learning and deep learning?, provide a practical course-related example and state one validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to classification; Machine learning lifecycle; Different applications of ML; Difference between AI and machine learning Machine Learning and deep learning?. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundametals of Machine Learning task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Supervised learning uses labelled examples. Regression predicts numeric targets and classification predicts discrete classes; validation is required to estimate generalization.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Advantage and disadvantage of supervised learning; Regressions- Linear regression; regression trees; on-linear regression and polynomial regression. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundametals of Machine Learning task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Supervised learning uses labelled examples. Regression predicts numeric targets and classification predicts discrete classes; validation is required to estimate generalization.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Types of unsupervised learning; Clustering algorithm k- means and KNN(k-nearest neighbors); Hierarchical clustering; anomaly’s detection. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Fundametals of Machine Learning task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

